window.__finlexDocLoaded(10209,{"id":10209,"articles":[{"id":1000872,"no":"Overview","heading":"Scope & Core Objective (Public Summary)","text":"Establishes recognition and disclosure rules for loss contingencies (ASC 450-20) and gain contingencies (ASC 450-30), using the higher US GAAP 'probable' threshold (~70%–75%+).","seq":0},{"id":1000873,"no":"ASC 450-20 / 30","heading":"Loss Contingencies (~75% Probable Bar, Range Minimum) & Gain Contingencies","text":"• Loss Contingency Accrual Criteria (ASC 450-20-25-2): Accrue a liability when BOTH (a) it is PROBABLE (likely to occur, ~70%–75%+ in US practice) that a liability has been incurred at the balance sheet date, AND (b) the amount of loss can be reasonably estimated.\n• Range of Loss (ASC 450-20-30-1): When a range of loss is estimable and NO amount within the range is a better estimate than any other, accrue the MINIMUM amount in the range and disclose the reasonably possible additional exposure up to the upper bound.\n• Reasonably Possible Losses (ASC 450-20-50-3~4): If loss is 'reasonably possible' (more than remote, less than probable), do NOT accrue — disclose the nature of contingency and estimated range of loss (or state an estimate cannot be made).\n• Discounting: Generally prohibited unless aggregate amount and timing of cash flows are fixed or reliably determinable.\n• Gain Contingencies (ASC 450-30): Never recognized prior to realization; avoid misleading disclosures.","seq":1},{"id":1000874,"no":"ASC 450 vs IAS 37 / CAS 13","heading":"Key Cross-Framework Divergences (75% vs. >50%; Minimum vs. Midpoint)","text":"• Recognition Threshold: ASC 450 'probable' (~70%–75%+) is materially higher than IAS 37 / CAS 13 'more likely than not' (>50%), delaying litigation/claim accruals under US GAAP.\n• Equal-Probability Range: ASC 450 accrues the MINIMUM of the range; IAS 37 / CAS 13 accrue the MIDPOINT (or expected value for large populations).\n• Discounting & Constructive Obligations: IAS 37 requires discounting when time value is material and covers constructive obligations broadly; ASC 450 generally prohibits discounting and focuses on legal/incurred obligations (restructuring exit costs sit separately in ASC 420).","seq":2},{"id":1000875,"no":"Official Access","heading":"Official FASB Codification & Reference Entry","text":"Official Portal (FASB Accounting Standards Codification®): https://asc.fasb.org/\nStatus: in_force (FASB ASC free Basic View available at https://asc.fasb.org/).","seq":3}]});
